  "stories": [
    {"id": "A01", "boundary": "Real R3 project and ownership", "required": ["Create a real customer and project through current HTTP; a direct project begins assessment with the authenticated personal owner and permanently consumed creator bootstrap.", "A real lead conversion with organizational ownership records the actual creator and inherited ownership origin. Only that creator with current membership may assign the first personal owner; concurrent attempts have one winner.", "After first assignment, returning to organization ownership does not restore creator privilege. Same-org unrelated actors, bare ProjectWrite and arbitrary platform roles do not obtain project scope.", "Reassignment and handover preparation check pre-change responsibility. Minimal creator response cannot expose full protected project facts."]},
    {"id": "A02", "boundary": "Contract, receipts and handover", "required": ["Produce real technical cost, bid/commercial and pricing approval facts; prepare each contract independently, activate actual term snapshot and formal receivables.", "Confirm gross cash using an exact contract tax/currency basis; verify gross=net+tax and original immutable basis. A historical confirmed receipt may only certify an evidenced missing basis with CAS and reason, preserving cash, status and confirmedAt.", "Prepare the real handover under the old responsibility gate; each participant confirms only their actual duties; one person can cover multiple duties. No privileged user impersonation or synthetic confirmation row."]},
    {"id": "A03", "boundary": "Minimum roles and controlled stages", "required": ["No current role assignment is 200/null. Create a real role package; parse number tokens before f64, require exact millionths sum 1000000 and zero-weight reason; include accepted 1e-6 and rejected 1e-7/0.10000000000000001.", "Freeze through actual summary/confirmation evidence. Frozen participants cannot change parent assignment, participant identity or weights; moving zero-weight rows must also fail.", "Execution requires true confirmed handover and valid frozen roles from the same project chain. Acceptance requires actual execution and delivery evidence. Stale expected versions and historical advanced stages cannot fabricate admission."]},
    {"id": "A04", "boundary": "Actual cost sources and explicit accounting", "required": ["Use real E expense/labor/finance-source costs and F stage/tax/allocation producers; do not insert fabricated receiver cost rows or infer invoice/payment links.", "Preparation enumerates the complete current source set. Include/exclude classification needs actual reasons, expected versions and evidence; missing or changed inputs fail before publication.", "Shared allocations conserve selected gross/net/tax priority and exact cents including deterministic remainders. Deduplicate actual source chains and allocation source sets across direct/share roles; real installment payments stay distinct.", "Project estimate is adopted once, not copied once per contract. Currency must have actual source evidence; no guessed default or synthetic FX conversion."]},
    {"id": "A05", "boundary": "G capture and H rules", "required": ["Exercise all G9 and H8 using one outer transaction, pre-effect expectedInputHash and final factual sourceHash; evaluate reloads exactly the stored immutable context and publishes DMER/OSER/four independent stage bindings/reasons/summaries.", "Match all 11 frozen policy rules and exact boundaries; a project cost lower bound applies independently to each stage. No invented qualitative thresholds.", "Distinguish known zero, unknown/null, maturity and formal eligibility. Negative observed margin with immature or low receipts stays unknown/materiality review, with hard constraints retained. Test 20 percent receipt boundary without display rounding.", "Manual review appends an evidence overlay and new effective bindings; it cannot alter source facts, maturity or hard block. Frozen snapshot output references remain acyclic and are never filled back later.", "Test MAX=9999999999999999.99, MAX/MAX zero margin, one-cent receipt vs MAX cost, 13 percent tax split, one-cent aggregate overflow as atomic pre-INSERT422, and historical exact 1.2300 versus non-exact 1.2340.", "Pending tax on both G snapshot families and H evidence is null plus explicit knowledge when unknown, preserving legacy stored zero."
    ]},
    {"id": "A06", "boundary": "Real corrections and restatements", "required": ["Once consumed, ordinary E/F mutation fails. A true governed restatement invokes the real labor/allocation/stage/tax producer under a sealed internal permit, locks the complete affected project/source set, and rebuilds every applicable live/period endpoint.", "Consumed shared-source stage/tax corrections preserve actual batch weights and measurement, rebuild the whole real allocation batch and restate all affected project outputs; permission on one receiver is insufficient.", "Old snapshots, classifications, period roots and evidence remain immutable; current authorities move through explicit CAS. Existing legacy current baseline/period/frozen-role records block semantic conflicts before any unique-constraint error.", "Missing real producer for other receipt/payment/invoice corrections is explicitly blocked; no invented ledger or unsupported repair endpoint."
    ]},
    {"id": "A07", "boundary": "Final acceptance, completion, conditions and archive", "required": ["Stage acceptance cannot complete a whole project. A true final accepted decision allows completion; conditional acceptance records real condition owners, due dates and evidence and allows conditional completion.", "Only the logged-in condition owner can close their task through the exact parent/child route and double CAS. The own-task DTO contains only allowed anchors, their own conditions/evidence and aggregate parent status; no acceptance/parent evidence leak and no required full ProjectDetail load.", "Closing the last outstanding condition changes the server aggregate while leaving original conditional conclusion immutable. Concurrent closes cannot skip tasks or duplicate immutable closure.", "Pending conditions block archive. Archive, replace and void are terminal ancillary facts and cannot reopen stage or remove audit/evidence. Cross-parent IDs and different-project references fail."]},
    {"id": "A08", "boundary": "Security, UI and protocol", "required": ["Every route requires exact permission plus real current responsibility scope; compare owner, confirmed finance/business-admin duty, real participant, creator-bootstrap-only, own-condition-only and unrelated same/cross-org users.", "Sensitive raw financial/tax/explanation/next-action keys are literal null for every caller; only projection values carry authorized data. Transitive labor and unknown lineage use the strongest group. Required sensitive GET audit failure returns no payload.", "Real browser users complete minimal role/stage/cost/accounting/review/acceptance/condition/archive forms. Verify JSON and DOM masking, read-only/loading/missing basis/unknown/403/409 states, and actual generated-client requests.", "All 16 new modern write contracts plus supporting C basis request require the explicit input version. Rust rejects legacy/missing protocol422 and invalid modern shape400; Native modern422 is clearly labelled unsupported reference, legacy fixtures retain original schema and status."]}
  ],
  "transactionAndConcurrency": {"requiredWriteFaultInjection": "Inventory each actual necessary write family from implemented SQL/UoW and inject an actual one-hit failure, assert rollback of its business writes, then same-body no-fault retry; preserve raw evidence and distinguish precondition session touches.", "cases": ["source and project CAS", "two creator first assignments", "role freeze vs participant movement", "source correction vs capture", "complete affected-allocation project locks", "receipt basis vs original terms mutation", "two same/final condition closes", "period/current legacy and modern competing authorities"], "rowLockEvidence": "Use actual pg_stat_activity/locks or controlled barriers; a sequential pair of HTTP calls is not a race certificate."},
